h Freelancer</b><br /> <b>Worked On</b>: Night Horrors: Enemy Action, Night Horrors: The Tormented<br /> <b>Working On: </b>Nada at the moment. Hire me!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2737-thrazghul","name":"Thrazghul","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T15:01:12-07:00","id":878129,"title":"","content":"At least it wasn't enema.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T15:14:18-07:00","id":878152,"title":"","content":"I'm not done listening to it yet but there are some nice tidbits dropped. Thank Ian!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T16:14:11-07:00","id":878213,"title":"","content":"Can someone post a summary? Seems that i have some problems playing the podcast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5811-starkiller","name":"Starkiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T17:10:05-07:00","id":878251,"title":"","content":"What problems are you having? It is also available through itunes and google play, and if you look under the player on the site, you can directly download it as an mp3.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Rick A. Carroll - Onyx Path Freelancer</b><br /> <b>Worked On</b>: Night Horrors: Enemy Action, Night Horrors: The Tormented<br /> <b>Working On: </b>Nada at the moment. Hire me!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2737-thrazghul","name":"Thrazghul","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T07:22:39-07:00","id":878705,"title":"","content":"Highlights from Ian are:<br /> <br /> - The game is called the Trinity Continuum because of all the settings that are possible. The 3 main settings are something special and will be revealed closer to launch. I believe the three main settings of Aeon, Aberrant, and Adventure! are anchor points in the time continuum. The other settings are possibilities or alternates worth exploring. <br /> - The core rule book has a modern day setting with rules for creating Daredevils as PCs.<br /> - An ancient Greek setting called Aegis <br /> - They're throwing around the idea of a 50's era post nuclear setting like Fallout. <br /> - A setting between Aberrant and Aeon called Anima that is heavy on the brain tech like Total Recall, the new Robocop, and the Matrix.<br /> - Ian plans on producing a technology manual for Aeon and for Aberrant. He also said that the Aberrant tech manual would make everyone happy. Lots of Cyberpunk-esk items I believe. <br /> <br /> This is all I can remember off the top of my head. I was listening to it in the car on the way home from work yesterday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T05:17:12-07:00","id":880883,"title":"","content":"If they're pondering a setting between Adventure and Abberant they shouldn't really limit themselves to the 50s - they should cover the whole Cold War era from the 50s to the 80s. I mean, the Adventure setting also covers multiple decades (the 20s to the 40s) so it shouldn't be much of a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T09:15:59-07:00","id":881036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NullApostle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/877543-ian-aa-watson-teases-animus-and-talks-trinity-on-16miles2hell?p=880883#post880883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they're pondering a setting between Adventure and Abberant they shouldn't really limit themselves to the 50s - they should cover the whole Cold War era from the 50s to the 80s. I mean, the Adventure setting also covers multiple decades (the 20s to the 40s) so it shouldn't be much of a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the 50s is a good reference for atomic horror/drive-in era movies style fiction and weirdness, while the 60s to 80s do call a different type of imagery, much closer to Apocalypse Now, Rambo, Tom Clancy-style spy thrillers and a bunch of stuff that i suspect resonate even more with the modern day setting in the core book. Though that's more my take from what has been said so far, overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T12:12:04-07:00","id":881155,"title":"","content":"So the Aberrant tech manual will be focusing heavily on cybertech, this means that with the trinity core plus the aberrant tech manual we could play a cyberpunk game, that's wonderful! Too bad that according on my calculations we will have to wait at least 2-3 years to read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5811-starkiller","name":"Starkiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T04:27:49-07:00","id":881657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/877543-ian-aa-watson-teases-animus-and-talks-trinity-on-16miles2hell?p=881036#post881036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess the 50s is a good reference for atomic horror/drive-in era movies style fiction and weirdness, while the 60s to 80s do call a different type of imagery</div> </div> </div> </div>The same is true for the Adventure! era, though. The 30s were a very different decade compared to the 20s, a whole different kind of imagery was evoked. To say nothing of the early 40s which were defined by the war - it had next to no similarity to the 20s.<br /> <br /> If they managed to make a compelling game out of those three decades they can do the same with the 50s to 80s.<br /> <br /> IMO, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T10:13:53-07:00","id":881937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/877543-ian-aa-watson-teases-animus-and-talks-trinity-on-16miles2hell?p=881155#post881155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Aberrant tech manual will be focusing heavily on cybertech, this means that with the trinity core plus the aberrant tech manual we could play a cyberpunk game, that's wonderful! Too bad that according on my calculations we will have to wait at least 2-3 years to read it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be surprised if Cyberpunk possibilities were not part of Aeon, as that era lends itself to a tech manual / similar resource (and it'd be great to continue the theme of options excluding dragging Aberrant era stuff into Aeon / keep Aeon quantum free).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T11:12:31-07:00","id":881998,"title":"","content":"What I want to know is this: In a world with daredevils, mesmerists, and stalwarts shouldn't the second wolrd war be different? Unless their numbers were extremely low I just don't see how the allies and the axis wouldn't try to recruit, capture, or eliminate them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T12:02:26-07:00","id":882069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/877543-ian-aa-watson-teases-animus-and-talks-trinity-on-16miles2hell?p=881937#post881937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd be surprised if Cyberpunk possibilities were not part of Aeon, as that era lends itself to a tech manual / similar resource (and it'd be great to continue the theme of options excluding dragging Aberrant era stuff into Aeon / keep Aeon quantum free).</div> </div> </div> </div>With the focus that the Aeon setting has on biotech is more probable that the augmentations will be biological rather than mechanical (so biopunk?) besides Ian A. A. Watson in the podcast said that the enhancements in the Aberrant tech manual are for those baselines who are feeling inferior to the novas so i think that type of augmentations will be quantum free; anyway i am thinking that with both Aeon and Aberrant tech manuals a lot of possibilities are opening up for a cyberpunk campaign with maybe daredevils or baselines as protagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5811,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5811-starkiller","user":"Starkiller","date":". 05-04-2016, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5811-starkiller","name":"Starkiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T16:07:07-07:00","id":882318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/877543-ian-aa-watson-teases-animus-and-talks-trinity-on-16miles2hell?p=881998#post881998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I want to know is this: In a world with daredevils, mesmerists, and stalwarts shouldn't the second wolrd war be different? Unless their numbers were extremely low I just don't see how the allies and the axis wouldn't try to recruit, capture, or eliminate them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume the same as superhero comics have, both sides had them, so the net effect balances out. Even if specific events would have occurred a bit differently here and there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T07:17:24-07:00","id":882842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/877543-ian-aa-watson-teases-animus-and-talks-trinity-on-16miles2hell?p=882069#post882069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the focus that the Aeon setting has on biotech is more probable that the augmentations will be biological rather than mechanical (so biopunk?) besides Ian A. A. Watson in the podcast said that the enhancements in the Aberrant tech manual are for those baselines who are feeling inferior to the novas so i think that type of augmentations will be quantum free; anyway i am thinking that with both Aeon and Aberrant tech manuals a lot of possibilities are opening up for a cyberpunk campaign with maybe daredevils or baselines as protagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I like about Aeon is I can make psi, hardtech, biotech and so on more or less important depending on my preferences with ease - so while biotech is a component, its never been the focus of Aeon for me. But yeah, I could see that working but prefer to be able to buy only Aeon books, without needed to dip into Aberrant, Anima or whatever books for stuff that the Aeon setting should provide. So long as I get plenty of new Aeon 2123+ specific era hardtech (as well as biotech options which I'd expect would be available) in a hypothetical Aeon tech manual I'm good <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T08:15:15-07:00","id":882881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/877543-ian-aa-watson-teases-animus-and-talks-trinity-on-16miles2hell?p=882842#post882842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I like about Aeon is I can make psi, hardtech, biotech and so on more or less important depending on my preferences with ease - so while biotech is a component, its never been the focus of Aeon for me. But yeah, I could see that working but prefer to be able to buy only Aeon books, without needed to dip into Aberrant, Anima or whatever books for stuff that the Aeon setting should provide. So long as I get plenty of new Aeon 2123+ specific era hardtech (as well as biotech options which I'd expect would be available) in a hypothetical Aeon tech manual I'm good <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would think that the tech manuals for each of the main settings in the Trinity would blend into the other &quot;in between&quot; continuum settings. For instance, the Aberrant tech manual would be useful for the Anima setting and so forth. Ian didn't mention it, probably because it's too far out, but I would love to see an Adventure! tech manual. I bet there would be some crazy stuff in there!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T10:24:16-07:00","id":882984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>karpomatic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/877543-ian-aa-watson-teases-animus-and-talks-trinity-on-16miles2hell?p=882881#post882881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think that the tech manuals for each of the main settings in the Trinity would blend into the other &quot;in between&quot; continuum settings. For instance, the Aberrant tech manual would be useful for the Anima setting and so forth. Ian didn't mention it, probably because it's too far out, but I would love to see an Adventure! tech manual. I bet there would be some crazy stuff in there!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sure - that would make sense. I'm just expressing a preference to purchase Aeon specific content. I actively dislike the Aberrant setting, Novas etc and am indifferent to the Adventure! setting; preferring not to need to buy hypothetical books from those settings to re-use in Aeon for content that should arguably be in an Aeon focussed supplement (which is different than using those books for in-between the settings, of course). I'd love to see the Trinity Tech manual revisited (preferably with zero mentions of novas, quantum et al).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T09:39:49-07:00","id":885430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/877543-ian-aa-watson-teases-animus-and-talks-trinity-on-16miles2hell?p=882318#post882318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would assume the same as superhero comics have, both sides had them, so the net effect balances out. Even if specific events would have occurred a bit differently here and there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially at the end of the war when Daredevil Otto Skorzeny, Mesmerist Heinrich Himmler, and Mad Scientist Joseph Mengela all escape and found Totally-Not-HYDRA...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T03:39:36-07:00","id":886081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/877543-ian-aa-watson-teases-animus-and-talks-trinity-on-16miles2hell?p=881937#post881937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd be surprised if Cyberpunk possibilities were not part of Aeon, as that era lends itself to a tech manual / similar resource (and it'd be great to continue the